llvm-4.0.0 backport patch: an array subscript's index is emitted before its base, as before r282453 (PS4)

This patch CHANGES CODE GENERATION in clang's
CodeGenFunction::EmitArraySubscriptExpr. clang r282453 (llvm-project
9e67b9922bb1, 2016-09-26, C++17's evaluation order for subscripts,
first release 4.0.0) emits the index after the base where the base is
written first. Before it the index is emitted, checked and promoted
before any base. With the base's field address emitted after the index,
SimplifyCFG hoists the address GVN's scalar PRE left in a split edge
and the edge block disappears: 0x13ace60 is equal to the base in the
prebuilt 3.7.1's module and 27 of 63 under this line without the patch
(round 233B); round 196B's first witness had held the candidate. With
the patch 0x13ace60 compiles to the base's bytes, 0xc19ab0 goes from
1 of 23 to 5 of 24, those are the only two functions of the rebuilt
module that change, and no matched game row changes (round 233B built
the front end, rebuilt the module from every unit and swept this
unconditional form alone).

diff -ru a/tools/clang/lib/CodeGen/CGExpr.cpp b/tools/clang/lib/CodeGen/CGExpr.cpp
--- a/tools/clang/lib/CodeGen/CGExpr.cpp
+++ b/tools/clang/lib/CodeGen/CGExpr.cpp
@@ -2935,30 +2935,15 @@
 
